    "description": "The Admin Control Plane performs role grants, policy changes, and signing-key rotations through the Configuration Service. The current workers append JSON lines to a local file, can rotate that file, and run with enough permission to rewrite or remove earlier records. Security and Internal Audit must be able to prove after an incident that privileged activity was attributable and that no event was silently deleted, reordered, or truncated. The records must include denied and failed attempts as well as successful changes. A separate Verification Service must be able to validate the history without trusting the worker that produced it, and the key used to authenticate records must not be stored beside the writable event file. A managed evidence store is not available, so the design must define how records are written, linked, and independently checked across multiple files and rotations.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose whether to replace privileged-activity files with a verifiable event sequence whose integrity can be checked independently by a party that cannot rewrite the source records.",
    "notes": "Malleable local files must become a verifiable sequence checkable by a party that cannot rewrite it; audit-interceptor is the near miss for the capture-at-boundary framing."
  },
